    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13039" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēmōlītĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		demolior, <i>no.</i> II., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a tearing down,
				demolishing</i> (very rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dum ea demolitio (statuarum) fieret,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Verr. 2, 2, 67</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10, 19</span></i>.— *
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">veritatis,</span>”
				<i>an undermining</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 2, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
